If $x+A > R$, then all reachable squares are $> R$, so we have jumped over the bad interval.
If $[x+A, x+B]$ overlaps with $[L, R]$, we can reach some squares in $[x+A, L-1]$ (if any) and some squares in $[R+1, x+B]$ (if any).
