Let $C$ be the common marginal cost. Then $2x_i P_i \approx C$. So $x_i \approx \frac{C}{2 P_i}$.
Then $\sum x_i \approx \sum \frac{C}{2 P_i} = \frac{C}{2} \sum \frac{1}{P_i}$.
